ls .mailmap 2>&1 || true
FINAL ANSWER:
Ownership of `src/` is highly concentrated: Andrew Gallant holds 76.9% of the surviving lines, so the bus factor is 1.

I counted with `git blame -w -M -C` at HEAD. That covers 7 files and 3,322 lines. Bus factor here means the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50% of the lines counted.

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits | Commit share |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Andrew Gallant | 2,554 | 76.9% | 55 | 51.9% |
| Ola Berg | 113 | 3.4% | 2 | 1.9% |
| Sebastian Thiel | 74 | 2.2% | 1 | 0.9% |
| Ashley | 68 | 2.0% | 1 | 0.9% |
| Aron Griffis | 59 | 1.8% | 1 | 0.9% |

28 more authors hold the remaining lines, each with 45 lines (1.4%) or fewer.

- **Bus factor:** 1 to reach 50%, scoped to `src/`. To reach 80% it takes 2 authors, on the same scope.
- **Excluded:** `src/errno_table.rs` (883 lines) is left out of every number because it is a generated file. `--keep-generated` would count it.
- **Reformat commit:** `c584a1d` ("style: switch to rustfmt", by Gallant) touched most of the files in `src/` and has 122 surviving lines. The tool did not set it aside automatically, so I checked it by re-running with `--ignore-rev c584a1d`. Gallant then has 2,547 lines (76.7%). The conclusion does not change.
- **Copy detection:** the figures use `-w -M -C`. Without copy detection, Gallant has 2,705 lines (81.4%). Garrett Berg drops from 34 lines (1.0%) to 0, and Niv Kaminer from 45 lines (1.4%) to 15 (0.5%).
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked for them. `c584a1d` is the only candidate, and it is the commit above.
- **Possible duplicate identity:** Ashley (`<email redacted>`, 68 lines) and Ashley Mannix (`<email redacted>`, 4 lines) may be the same person. The evidence is weak and rests only on name and address, so I kept them separate. If they are one person, that is 72 lines (2.2%), which does not change the bus factor. There is no `.mailmap` in the repo, and I did not write one.

Surviving lines show whose code is still there. They do not show who understands it, who reviewed it, or which code was deleted on purpose.

